111
00:03:35,227 --> 00:03:36,907
The reason we called you here today

112
00:03:37,737 --> 00:03:40,467
was to ask you about an important matter

113
00:03:40,467 --> 00:03:43,117
that we can't publicly reveal for safety reasons.

114
00:03:43,627 --> 00:03:45,207
And that is?

115
00:03:45,207 --> 00:03:47,167
The Imperial Capital Recapture Operation.

116
00:03:48,657 --> 00:03:53,427
By the looks of it, the former empire's remaining 
loyalists have gathered and are planning something.

117
00:03:53,427 --> 00:03:59,177
If recall correctly, their leader's name was Ragreed Forus.

118
00:04:00,437 --> 00:04:02,007
Ragreed Forus!

119
00:04:02,007 --> 00:04:06,437
They are going to execute their plan right after the All Dragons Battle

120
00:04:06,437 --> 00:04:09,127
that will be held during the Kingdom Founding Festival.

121
00:04:09,127 --> 00:04:14,337
They want to strike while our guards
 are spread to their thinnest.

122
00:04:14,337 --> 00:04:17,217
So what do you want me to do?

123
00:04:17,217 --> 00:04:21,157
We want you to be our secret weapon against this Imperial Capital Recapture Operation.

124
00:04:21,777 --> 00:04:26,277
According to our spies, in an abandoned village in the northwest of the kingdom,

125
00:04:26,277 --> 00:04:29,517
there are about a hundred Abysses hiding in wait.

126
00:04:29,517 --> 00:04:30,627
A hundred?!

127
00:04:31,007 --> 00:04:32,967
Is that certain?

128
00:04:32,967 --> 00:04:34,137
Yes.

129
00:04:34,137 --> 00:04:40,407
There is little doubt that the Abysses are
 being held there by the power of the horn.

130
00:04:40,407 --> 00:04:44,807
We need to take them out
 before the rebels make their move.

131
00:04:44,807 --> 00:04:48,047
For that purpose, Lux Arcadia,

132
00:04:48,047 --> 00:04:52,897
we want you to bait out
 those hundred Abysses.

133
00:04:52,897 --> 00:04:57,607
Th-This is too much, Prime Minister Nalf!

134
00:04:57,607 --> 00:04:59,587
Not even my brother can 
stand alone against that many!

135
00:04:59,587 --> 00:05:02,047
The incident at Ries Island.

136
00:05:02,867 --> 00:05:08,167
If you do this for us, we will turn a blind eye to the transgressions

137
00:05:08,167 --> 00:05:13,587
of your headmistress, Relie Aingram,
 and your knight squadron.

138
00:05:14,247 --> 00:05:17,047
I think it's a good deal for you.

139
00:05:17,557 --> 00:05:18,557
How about it?

140
00:05:22,007 --> 00:05:23,457
But...

141
00:05:24,517 --> 00:05:25,527
I accept.

142
00:05:26,477 --> 00:05:27,947
Lux!

143
00:05:27,947 --> 00:05:29,837
We forgot to mention,

144
00:05:30,437 --> 00:05:34,007
but please keep in mind you are to also win the All Dragons Battle.

145
00:05:34,007 --> 00:05:35,097
Win?

146
00:05:35,097 --> 00:05:36,257
Yes.

147
00:05:36,257 --> 00:05:41,107
It's the least we expect to compensate for
 the trouble this transgression has caused us.

148
00:05:41,637 --> 00:05:43,657
That's beyond unreasonable!

149
00:05:43,657 --> 00:05:44,907
Airi.

150
00:05:45,467 --> 00:05:47,617
I'll be all right.

151
00:05:49,487 --> 00:05:51,837
You're too softhearted!

152
00:05:52,397 --> 00:05:54,517
I'm sorry, Airi.

153
00:05:55,837 --> 00:05:57,547
Prime Minister Nalf.

154
00:05:57,547 --> 00:06:05,217
I accept both tasks. Baiting out the Abysses
 and winning the tournament.

155
00:06:08,807 --> 00:06:12,767
The planning meeting for the Abysses extermination took quite a while.

156
00:06:15,517 --> 00:06:16,687
Are you cold?

157
00:06:16,687 --> 00:06:17,807
Put this on.

158
00:06:17,807 --> 00:06:19,257
No!

159
00:06:19,257 --> 00:06:20,197
Jeez!

160
00:06:21,097 --> 00:06:23,637
Thank you for worrying for me.

161
00:06:23,637 --> 00:06:24,207
Butâ

162
00:06:24,207 --> 00:06:29,537
Why didn't you tell them 
that you can't use Bahamut?

163
00:06:29,537 --> 00:06:30,417
Huh?

164
00:06:30,827 --> 00:06:34,377
You do remember how long you can use Bahamut for, don't you?

165
00:06:34,377 --> 00:06:37,577
Twelve minutes, right?

166
00:06:37,577 --> 00:06:39,027
I know.

167
00:06:39,027 --> 00:06:41,587
Still, someone has to do it.

168
00:06:41,587 --> 00:06:45,007
I'm certain I can find a way.

169
00:06:47,477 --> 00:06:49,807
That's how things always end up.

170
00:06:50,397 --> 00:06:56,277
I thought I could protect you a bit,
 if I came along.

171
00:06:59,117 --> 00:07:00,197
Lux?

172
00:07:00,697 --> 00:07:04,697
I'm sorry I always worry you so much.

173
00:07:18,807 --> 00:07:20,007
What's that about?

174
00:07:20,437 --> 00:07:23,717
How would that change anything?

175
00:07:23,717 --> 00:07:25,367
I don't know.

176
00:07:25,367 --> 00:07:30,557
I can't be certain it will help,
 but could you do it all the same?

177
00:07:32,567 --> 00:07:35,927
And you want the machine to have the same performance as usual?

178
00:07:35,927 --> 00:07:37,317
Can you do that?

179
00:07:38,727 --> 00:07:40,667
I think I can manage it.

180
00:07:40,667 --> 00:07:45,127
I'm actually pretty good at
 such seemingly useless stuff.

181
00:07:45,127 --> 00:07:47,677
That you very much, Miss Lisha.

182
00:07:48,597 --> 00:07:49,577
Don't mention it.

183
00:07:49,577 --> 00:07:56,607
A-Anyway, let's take the victory at the All Dragons Battle tomorrow!

184
00:07:56,607 --> 00:07:57,547
Yes!

185
00:08:04,047 --> 00:08:05,077
<i>Was that her?</i>

186
00:08:14,117 --> 00:08:15,317
I knew it.

187
00:08:16,237 --> 00:08:19,157
Long time no see, Master.

188
00:08:19,157 --> 00:08:21,597
I'm honored to meet you again.

189
00:08:26,167 --> 00:08:29,077
You should be a little more careful.

190
00:08:29,077 --> 00:08:34,397
As the only male survivor of the Arcadia imperial family,

191
00:08:34,397 --> 00:08:37,667
you should keep capable guards.

192
00:08:39,337 --> 00:08:43,417
I'd be more than happy to answer any questions you have for me.

193
00:08:43,417 --> 00:08:47,637
I don't have any intention of fighting you tonight, Master.

194
00:08:48,677 --> 00:08:53,117
Yoruka, last time you said you fight
 because of the pact you made, right?

195
00:08:53,117 --> 00:08:53,917
Yes.

196
00:08:55,017 --> 00:09:00,777
Why are you still trying to uphold that pact,
 even though the empire is no more?

197
00:09:01,527 --> 00:09:03,997
In order to keep a promise.

198
00:09:03,997 --> 00:09:05,317
To my brother.

199
00:09:05,697 --> 00:09:07,217
Your brother?

200
00:09:07,217 --> 00:09:08,027
Yes.

201
00:09:08,657 --> 00:09:13,287
Since I was a child, I've had a certain talent.

202
00:09:13,717 --> 00:09:20,427
The talent to sense people's killing intent,
 and kill then without hesitation.

203
00:09:20,427 --> 00:09:21,497
Huh?

204
00:09:21,497 --> 00:09:25,967
My father called me a "heartless monster".

205
00:09:28,007 --> 00:09:33,997
He died of an illness, so my twin brother inherited the throne at a young age.

206
00:09:33,997 --> 00:09:40,437
Unlike me, he was a sickly child,
 but he had a decent human heart.

207
00:09:41,237 --> 00:09:45,727
He protected the kingdom and its people,
 and also wanted to protect me,

208
00:09:45,727 --> 00:09:48,407
despite everyone detesting me.

209
00:09:48,937 --> 00:09:52,757
But your kingdom was destroyed by the empire.

210
00:09:54,317 --> 00:09:59,087
Did my father force you into that pact
 by taking your brother hostage?

211
00:10:00,667 --> 00:10:07,137
I mean no disrespect, but you, Master,
 are much like my brother.

212
00:10:07,137 --> 00:10:11,547
Though your hair and the color of your eyes...
 Everything about you looks quite different.

213
00:10:13,237 --> 00:10:16,167
My brother was killed long ago.

214
00:10:16,167 --> 00:10:16,817
Huh?

215
00:10:16,817 --> 00:10:18,017
Then...

216
00:10:18,437 --> 00:10:23,867
I cannot break the pact
 I made for my brother.

217
00:10:23,867 --> 00:10:28,737
That's the only way to show
 my loyalty to my dead brother.

218
00:10:29,357 --> 00:10:35,757
I intend to destroy this new kingdom
 in order to fulfill my pact with your father.

219
00:10:37,497 --> 00:10:42,027
Now, I would like to have your answer, Master.

220
00:10:42,027 --> 00:10:45,587
What are your plans for this kingdom?

221
00:10:47,047 --> 00:10:48,627
I...

222
00:10:48,627 --> 00:10:51,807
Despite all that, I can't go along with your intent.

223
00:10:52,757 --> 00:10:53,877
Becauseâ

224
00:10:54,937 --> 00:10:59,697
It's unfortunate that you and I
 have to be enemies, Master.

225
00:11:02,587 --> 00:11:06,437
Please be careful during
 tomorrow's All Dragons Battle.

226
00:11:06,437 --> 00:11:10,397
I'd hate to see you die
 by someone else's hand.

227
00:11:23,417 --> 00:11:26,477
Everyone, I thank you for your help at Ries Island.

228
00:11:26,477 --> 00:11:31,527
But today, you're here to win for the
 new kingdom and for your own sakes.

229
00:11:31,527 --> 00:11:32,467
You got that?

230
00:11:32,837 --> 00:11:33,677
Yes, ma'am!

231
00:11:36,087 --> 00:11:40,107
<i>And so, the two days of the All Dragons Battle began.</i>

232
00:11:41,217 --> 00:11:44,377
<i>The matches on the first day are one-on-one.</i>

233
00:11:44,377 --> 00:11:46,247
<i>Team battles are held on the second day.</i>

234
00:11:46,247 --> 00:11:49,067
<i>In the end, the points each team earns on both days are totaled.</i>

235
00:11:51,177 --> 00:11:55,517
<i>We, the new kingdom's team, lost our first match,</i>

236
00:11:55,517 --> 00:12:02,127
<i>but Celes, Philuffy, and Krulcifer
 won the next three.</i><i></i><i></i>

237
00:12:02,127 --> 00:12:06,247
<i>If my brother and Miss Lisha
 win the two remaining matches,</i>

238
00:12:06,247 --> 00:12:09,097
<i>we'd be in the lead at the end of the first day.</i>

239
00:12:10,777 --> 00:12:12,087
Miss Lisha?

240
00:12:12,597 --> 00:12:13,937
How is Tillfur?

241
00:12:13,937 --> 00:12:15,127
She's fine.

242
00:12:15,127 --> 00:12:17,887
Her Machine Dragon is pretty broken down,
 but she herself is uninjured.

243
00:12:17,887 --> 00:12:19,437
How is Lux doing?

244
00:12:19,437 --> 00:12:22,097
His opponent is quite a tough one.

245
00:12:22,427 --> 00:12:25,817
But I think it will be over any moment now.

246
00:12:31,277 --> 00:12:32,697
Howling Roar!

247
00:12:39,327 --> 00:12:40,577
Match over!

248
00:12:41,907 --> 00:12:44,687
Contestant judged to be
 unable to continue fighting.

249
00:12:44,687 --> 00:12:46,777
Winner: Lux Arcadia.

250
00:12:47,877 --> 00:12:51,537
Another splendid victory
 for our Undefeated Weakest.

251
00:12:51,537 --> 00:12:52,717
Was it really?

252
00:12:52,717 --> 00:12:53,967
What?

253
00:12:53,967 --> 00:12:58,257
He has that title because he saves his special techniques for when it really matters,

254
00:12:58,257 --> 00:13:02,317
and just lets time run out in matches such as these.

255
00:13:03,157 --> 00:13:07,097
But this time, he looked like he was in a hurry to win.

256
00:13:07,097 --> 00:13:08,407
It's not like him.

257
00:13:11,957 --> 00:13:12,957
Lux!

258
00:13:13,857 --> 00:13:15,067
Airi!

259
00:13:16,437 --> 00:13:18,607
You didn't have a chance to rest after the match.

260
00:13:18,607 --> 00:13:20,467
Didn't it wear you out?

261
00:13:20,467 --> 00:13:22,477
No. I'm okay.

262
00:13:22,477 --> 00:13:23,707
Thank you.

263
00:13:23,707 --> 00:13:29,077
If I don't manage to get back for the team battle tomorrow, tell the others I wish them luck.

264
00:13:29,077 --> 00:13:30,287
Okay.

265
00:13:30,287 --> 00:13:33,257
All right, Airi, I'm leaving the rest to you.

266
00:13:33,717 --> 00:13:36,217
Come back safely, Lux.

267
00:13:36,217 --> 00:13:37,247
I will.

268
00:13:41,927 --> 00:13:41,927


269
00:13:46,507 --> 00:13:48,597
You're up next, Miss Lisha.

270
00:13:48,597 --> 00:13:49,807
Yes.

271
00:13:49,807 --> 00:13:52,817
I'll ride the momentum we have
 and snatch the win!

272
00:13:55,307 --> 00:13:55,777
All right!

273
00:13:56,517 --> 00:13:57,807
Good luck!

274
00:13:57,807 --> 00:13:58,587
Thanks.

275
00:14:03,347 --> 00:14:06,997
<i>I hope everything goes well...</i>

276
00:14:09,087 --> 00:14:11,707
<i>Miss Lisha's match began.</i>

277
00:14:11,707 --> 00:14:17,467
<i>For a while it was an even battle,
 and the audience was hyped up.</i>

278
00:14:18,517 --> 00:14:21,257
<i>However, halfway through the battle,
 something went wrong.</i>

279
00:14:36,157 --> 00:14:38,357
Did something malfunction?

280
00:14:46,197 --> 00:14:47,607
W-Wait!

281
00:14:47,607 --> 00:14:49,157
I didn't do that!

282
00:14:50,427 --> 00:14:51,167
How?!

283
00:14:51,827 --> 00:14:52,877
Freezing Cannon!

284
00:15:05,637 --> 00:15:07,597
We'd like you to come with us.

285
00:15:07,597 --> 00:15:10,947
Y-You've got it wrong! This wasn't my fault!

286
00:15:10,947 --> 00:15:14,707
We'd like to keep you in custody until the investigation is over,

287
00:15:15,847 --> 00:15:19,107
Your Highness, Princess Lisesharte Atismata.

288
00:15:19,477 --> 00:15:21,567
Hear me out! I did do anything!

289
00:15:21,567 --> 00:15:23,117
You shouldn't argue here.

290
00:15:24,477 --> 00:15:27,537
Regardless of the circumstances, this is not the time and place.

291
00:15:55,647 --> 00:15:57,937
Sharp as ever, I see, fallen prince.

292
00:15:58,517 --> 00:16:02,797
Not only do you not run after being ambushed,
 but you immediately strike back.

293
00:16:02,797 --> 00:16:04,907
Are you the one controlling the Abysses here?

294
00:16:05,277 --> 00:16:08,007
I'll have my revenge on you
 for beating me on the island.

295
00:16:36,147 --> 00:16:36,767
I made it!

296
00:16:45,237 --> 00:16:46,867
We're a stone's throw from the capital!

297
00:16:47,477 --> 00:16:49,777
Don't let a single one pass!

298
00:16:50,477 --> 00:16:52,187
Mission accomplished.

299
00:16:52,187 --> 00:16:54,117
Good work baiting them out.

300
00:16:54,117 --> 00:16:56,297
The rest is a battle of attrition.

301
00:16:56,297 --> 00:16:58,647
Get some rest for now.

302
00:16:58,647 --> 00:16:59,797
Yes, sir.

303
00:17:09,037 --> 00:17:13,567
I was wondering where Lux was,
 in this time of crisis for our princess.

304
00:17:14,557 --> 00:17:17,057
He's baiting out a large group
 of Abysses on his own?

305
00:17:17,477 --> 00:17:18,517
Yes.

306
00:17:18,517 --> 00:17:20,317
I'm sorry for not telling you.

307
00:17:20,317 --> 00:17:21,767
That's too reckless!

308
00:17:21,767 --> 00:17:23,437
We should join him!

309
00:17:23,437 --> 00:17:24,967
Please wait!

310
00:17:24,967 --> 00:17:30,807
One of the demands of the kingdom was
 to be victorious in the All Dragons Battle.

311
00:17:30,807 --> 00:17:34,977
If you drop out of the tournament, this will have been for nothing.

312
00:17:34,977 --> 00:17:38,207
It's all my fault, isn't it?

313
00:17:38,207 --> 00:17:41,047
He's doing it to make up for what Relie and I did.

314
00:17:41,047 --> 00:17:43,257
I don't think he sees it that way.

315
00:17:43,757 --> 00:17:47,977
Lux wants to protect all of you.

316
00:17:47,977 --> 00:17:50,057
That's his vice.

317
00:17:50,057 --> 00:17:52,217
He always bears everyone else's burdens.

318
00:17:53,527 --> 00:17:57,397
To reduce some of that burden,
 while he's fighting,

319
00:17:57,397 --> 00:18:02,187
we should do what we can about
 the situation we have at hand here.

320
00:18:02,697 --> 00:18:05,987
You're talking about Lisesharte's case, I assume.

321
00:18:05,987 --> 00:18:06,647
Yes.

322
00:18:07,137 --> 00:18:13,867
There's only one person who could have manipulated Miss Lisha's Machine Dragon.

323
00:18:14,237 --> 00:18:19,257
Yes. The Empire's Dagger, Kirihime Yoruka.

324
00:18:20,827 --> 00:18:26,257
The Divine Raiment of her Yato-no-kami
 is manipulation of other Machine Dragons.

325
00:18:26,957 --> 00:18:32,717
We need to find and capture her
 to prevent further incidents.

326
00:18:32,717 --> 00:18:35,727
And naturally, to save our princess.

327
00:18:38,797 --> 00:18:43,347
<i>Come to think of it, where did
 Saniya disappear to afterwards?</i>

328
00:18:44,547 --> 00:18:46,857
<i>Something's not right.</i>

329
00:18:48,037 --> 00:18:51,377
<i>I feel like we're overlooking something very important.</i>

330
00:19:05,047 --> 00:19:06,497
Hang in there!

331
00:19:06,497 --> 00:19:07,957
What happened?!

332
00:19:08,967 --> 00:19:10,707
It's the rebels.

333
00:19:10,707 --> 00:19:14,697
After the Abysses had worn us out, they attacked us.

334
00:19:14,697 --> 00:19:15,907
But...

335
00:19:15,907 --> 00:19:19,177
The rebel army was supposed to come
 after the tournament is over.

336
00:19:19,637 --> 00:19:21,347
<i>Ah, I get it now!</i>

337
00:19:21,347 --> 00:19:22,397
<i>That was their plan all along!</i>

338
00:19:22,767 --> 00:19:26,127
Our main forces have already retreated.

339
00:19:26,127 --> 00:19:30,127
Crossfeed will become the next battlefield.

340
00:19:37,027 --> 00:19:37,827
Did you find anything?

341
00:19:37,827 --> 00:19:39,267
We don't know where she is.

342
00:19:39,267 --> 00:19:41,237
It's almost dawn.

343
00:19:41,237 --> 00:19:42,047
Girls!

344
00:19:43,597 --> 00:19:47,417
Tomorrow's tournament was just canceled due to an emergency.

345
00:19:48,047 --> 00:19:49,377
What is the meaning of that?!

346
00:19:49,377 --> 00:19:52,377
The announcement said that an enemy force
 has broken through our defense line

347
00:19:53,117 --> 00:19:55,847
and is advancing toward us
 from the northwest.

348
00:19:57,617 --> 00:19:58,807
<i>Lux...</i>

349
00:20:03,837 --> 00:20:04,727
Him?!

350
00:20:05,857 --> 00:20:09,687
We meet again, Lux Arcadia!

351
00:20:10,667 --> 00:20:13,367
The capital <i>will</i> fall.

352
00:20:13,367 --> 00:20:19,907
And then, following the spirit of the former empire,
 I'll take the throne as the new emperor.

353
00:20:20,847 --> 00:20:22,467
I pity you.

354
00:20:22,467 --> 00:20:23,317
What?

355
00:20:23,317 --> 00:20:24,397
That large army behind you...

356
00:20:24,397 --> 00:20:27,267
Do you think they're all loyalists of the former empire?

357
00:20:27,267 --> 00:20:31,387
Most of them were definitely sent by a 
neighboring kingdom looking to take over Atismata.

358
00:20:31,387 --> 00:20:35,137
Can't you tell you're being used?!
 You're a puppet!

359
00:20:40,437 --> 00:20:41,807
A puppet?!

360
00:20:42,317 --> 00:20:44,017
Fine by me.

361
00:20:44,017 --> 00:20:48,267
As emperor, I'll be able to proudly
 brandish my power in this kingdom.

362
00:20:48,667 --> 00:20:51,737
I'll be able to do whatever I want with its assets and peasants.

363
00:20:51,737 --> 00:20:53,917
I'll tyrannize to my heart's content.

364
00:20:53,917 --> 00:20:55,907
That's enough for me.

365
00:20:57,987 --> 00:20:59,157
Over my dead body.

366
00:21:00,037 --> 00:21:01,947
You'll never have that!

367
00:21:03,617 --> 00:21:06,667
That's a bold statement from a fallen prince.

368
00:21:09,837 --> 00:21:14,117
What? Not going to use Bahamut on the likes of me?

369
00:21:14,117 --> 00:21:16,047
I'll let you in on a secret then.

370
00:21:17,047 --> 00:21:21,327
An even greater calamity is about to strike at the new kingdom.

371
00:21:21,327 --> 00:21:25,227
A force a Ragnarok can't compare to!

372
00:21:36,417 --> 00:21:37,887
What in the world is that?!

373
00:21:41,437 --> 00:21:45,367
The fifth ruin, The Giant.

374
00:21:48,157 --> 00:21:50,087
What are you going to do now?

375
00:21:50,087 --> 00:21:56,497
What <i>can</i> you do in that sad Wyvern against my army and that giant?!

376
00:21:58,537 --> 00:22:01,927
<i>You do remember how long you can use Bahamut for, don't you?</i><i></i>

377
00:22:03,317 --> 00:22:05,967
<i>I'll have to take my chances.</i>

378
